MoBetta: mtld3d: Keep the shader cache in %LOCALAPPDATA%\mtld3d-cache and turn it on for WoW.

athei/mtld3d v0.15.1 (9919759) keeps its shader and pipeline cache,
mtld3d_shaders.bin, beside the executable. Beside Wow.exe is the game
folder (MoBetta constraint 1), so patch 0002 turned the cache off in the
wow profile, and every launch compiled each shader and pipeline on first
use: up to 313 ms sync batches on arrival in Booty Bay and Dalaran
(MoBetta Session #27).

The cache now lives in the prefix, under
%LOCALAPPDATA%\mtld3d-cache\<exe stem>\mtld3d_shaders.bin (its .lock
sidecar beside it); the directory is created before the path is mapped,
since a directory that does not exist yet may have no unix path. Without
LOCALAPPDATA there is no cache rather than one in the executable's
directory. With that, the wow profile no longer turns the cache off;
mtld3d.conf and MTLD3D_CONFIG can still set shaderCache.enable=false.

